WEBVTT

00:00:00.315 --> 00:00:02.964
The fictional error case asks for two copies

00:00:03.054 --> 00:00:05.389
by Friday at two p.m., while another part

00:00:05.435 --> 00:00:07.994
says the meeting is Monday morning. No resolved

00:00:08.084 --> 00:00:11.088
date is supplied. Set the expected behavior before

00:00:11.402 --> 00:00:14.681
testing: flag the conflict and refer the deadline

00:00:14.905 --> 00:00:18.274
for human clarification. Do not let the assistant

00:00:18.364 --> 00:00:21.283
guess a date or invent a confirmation. Run

00:00:21.328 --> 00:00:24.708
the case and retain the actual response. Inspect

00:00:24.798 --> 00:00:27.314
the proposed action as well as the wording.

00:00:27.583 --> 00:00:29.604
If it assigns a final route using an

00:00:29.648 --> 00:00:33.421
invented deadline, record the defect, revise the fictional

00:00:33.556 --> 00:00:37.328
rule and retest. Keep the unresolved question visible

00:00:37.508 --> 00:00:39.858
until appropriate evidence resolves it.
